<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Parameter study of <math id="A3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math></h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To further understand the impact of the parameter <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>, we’ve conducted parameter experiments to observe the effects of varying <math id="A3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> values under different tasks. The experimental results are shown in the Table <a href="#A2.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ Appendix B Derivation of Formulas ‣ TCPO: Thought-Centric Preference Optimization forEffective Embodied Decision-making" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>. It can be seen that <math id="A3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">kappa</annotation></semantics></math>=0.1 achieves the best performance across all tasks in ALFWorld.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Pseudo Code of TCPO</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We present the pseudo code of TCPO below for better understanding of our approach.</p><span class="ltx_rule ltx_align_center" style="width:100%;height:0.8pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>
<p id="A4.p1.2" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left ltx_align_center"><span id="A4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> Training pipeline of embodied VLMs thorogh TCPO</p><span class="ltx_rule ltx_align_center" style="width:100%;height:1px;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>
<div id="A4.p1.3" class="ltx_listing ltx_align_center ltx_listing">
<div id="algx1.l0" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">0:</span>
            
            
           Reference policy network <math id="algx1.l0.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{ref}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{ref}</annotation></semantics></math>, finetune policy network <math id="algx1.l0.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, current observation <math id="algx1.l0.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, past trajectories wises buffer <math id="algx1.l0.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{i}^{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{i}^{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="algx1.l0.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{i=1\dots N\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{i=1\dots N\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
           <span id="algx1.l1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="algx1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,2,...,N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,2,...,N</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algx1.l1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="algx1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
            Randomly sample past trajectory <math id="algx1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{i}^{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{i}^{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. The current chain of reasoning thoughts <math id="algx1.l2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}(\mathcal{T}_{i}^{t}|\tau_{i}^{t-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}(\mathcal{T}_{i}^{t}|\tau_{i}^{t-1})</annotation></semantics></math> and probabilities of output actions <math id="algx1.l2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(a_{i}^{t}|\mathcal{T}_{i}^{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(a_{i}^{t}|\mathcal{T}_{i}^{t})</annotation></semantics></math> are generated through previous trajectories and fine-tuned models. <math id="algx1.l2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{ref}(a_{i}^{t},\mathcal{T}_{i}^{t}|\tau_{i}^{t-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{ref}(a_{i}^{t},\mathcal{T}_{i}^{t}|\tau_{i}^{t-1})</annotation></semantics></math> is also obtained through the reference model.

</div>
<div id="algx1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
            <span id="algx1.l3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="algx1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> in past trajectories buffer which can be paired with <math id="algx1.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{i}^{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{i}^{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. <span id="algx1.l3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="algx1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
             The current chain of reasoning thoughts <math id="algx1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}(\mathcal{T}_{j}^{t}|\tau_{j}^{t-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}(\mathcal{T}_{j}^{t}|\tau_{j}^{t-1})</annotation></semantics></math> and probabilities of output actions <math id="algx1.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(a_{j}^{t}|\mathcal{T}_{j}^{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(a_{j}^{t}|\mathcal{T}_{j}^{t})</annotation></semantics></math> are generated through previous trajectories and fine-tuned models. <math id="algx1.l4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{ref}(a_{j}^{t},\mathcal{T}_{j}^{t}|\tau_{j}^{t-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{ref}(a_{j}^{t},\mathcal{T}_{j}^{t}|\tau_{j}^{t-1})</annotation></semantics></math> is also obtained through the reference model.

</div>
<div id="algx1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
             Calculating the loss in Equtation <a href="#S3.E6" title="In 3.2 Preference Fine-Tuning with CoT ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ TCPO: Thought-Centric Preference Optimization forEffective Embodied Decision-making" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>.

</div>
<div id="algx1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
            <span id="algx1.l6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="algx1.l6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="algx1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
            Compute the Regularization loss <math id="algx1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{L_{2}}\left(\pi_{\theta}(a_{1}^{t}|\mathcal{T}_{1}^{t}),\pi_{\text{ref}}(a_{1}^{t}|\mathcal{T}_{1}^{t})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{L_{2}}\left(\pi_{\theta}(a_{1}^{t}|\mathcal{T}_{1}^{t}),\pi_{\text{ref}}(a_{1}^{t}|\mathcal{T}_{1}^{t})\right)</annotation></semantics></math> and obtain the <math id="algx1.l7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{TCPO}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>TCPO</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{TCPO}}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="algx1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
           <span id="algx1.l8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="algx1.l8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="algx1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
           The parameters <math id="algx1.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> are updated by backpropagation through the loss function.

</div>
</div><span class="ltx_rule ltx_align_center" style="width:100%;height:1px;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>
</div>
